{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/12997-size-of-swarms","id":12997,"title":"Size of Swarms?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2013-11-17T15:23:17-08:00","id":12997,"title":"Size of Swarms?","content":"So, I looked at the swarm powers. They seem pretty cool, but how big are the swarms they make?<br /> <br /> For reference:<br /> Swarm -- Page 269<br /> Insect Swarm -- Page 315","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-28T12:51:49-08:00","id":19863,"title":"","content":"For the Swarm exploit, I think the Swarm's maximum size would depend on the demon's Primum. Assuming that the damage that the single-target swarm inflicts is equivalent to the damage the swarm should inflict when condensed to a 1 yard radius, the formula in the Swarm Tilt gets a maximum area of \u03c02<sup>2(Primum-1)</sup> yards.<br /> <br /> I have no idea about the Insect Swarm form ability. Perhaps it could use the same guidelines as the Exploit? That would make them almost identical, with the form ability being a little easier to use while the Exploit's a little more powerful and versatile.<br /> <br /> Math nitpick: \u03c0(r/2)<sup>2</sup> = (1/4)\u03c0r<sup>2</sup> \u2260 (1/2)\u03c0r<sup>2</sup>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1231,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1231-gapb","user":"gapb","date":".  Clarification. 11-28-2013, 03:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1231-gapb","name":"gapb","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"23"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-16T12:15:22-08:00","id":31110,"title":"","content":"Caution! Math!<br /> <br /> @gapb's idea and equation are right, however in case you're curious about the volume:<br /> The damage is each doubling of the radius in yards, or: Damage = log<sub>2</sub>(maximum size radius in yards) + 1 (Since a 1-yard radius is 2<sup>0</sup>, and the baseline is 1 damage at a 1-yard radius)<br /> From the Swarm Exploit, Damage = Primium. To get the logarithm out, you subtract one from both sides and have both sides be the power of 2. (Since the logarithm is base-2)<br /> Therefore, Maximum size radius in yards = 2<sup>Primium-1</sup><br /> <br /> The volume of the sphere of a swarm of bees or seagulls (or etc.) would be (4/3)*\u03c0*r<sup>3</sup>, or slightly more than 2<sup>3*Primium-1</sup> cubic yards.<br /> <br /> So even at Primum 1, you can have a swarm just over 4 cubic yards, (the volume of most dumpsters!), while at Primum 10 (or when going loud!) you can have a swarm 562,209,904 cubic yards in volume (enough to blanket the District of Columbia almost 3 yards deep, if your ST allows shaping the swarm like that.)<br /> <br /> (For scale, and apparently because I'm <i>that guy</i>, at Primum 15 you could have a swarm that blanketed the continental United States almost 2 yards deep, doing 1 bashing damage per turn)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Once is happenstance. Twice is coincidence. Three times is enemy action. Four times is Infrastructure.<br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><br /> Rule #2: Never let the game-mechanics get in the way of a good story.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1642-paddon","name":"Paddon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1642_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"326"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-16T12:40:40-08:00","id":31131,"title":"","content":"As for the volume of the Insect Swarm form, let's assume the total volume is the same as the character's human body. According to Wolfram Alpha, the average human body (A 146 lb dude) is 66.4 liters, or 0.0868 cubic yards. As a sphere radius, that puts it at just smaller than 10-inches. (doing the math, you'd have to be over 260 lb to get a 1-foot radius sphere) Personally, better to go with what gapb said, and assume the Swarm Exploit volume for the swarm size of Insect Form.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Once is happenstance. Twice is coincidence. Three times is enemy action. Four times is Infrastructure.<br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><br /> Rule #2: Never let the game-mechanics get in the way of a good story.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1642-paddon","name":"Paddon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1642_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"326"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-16T12:56:55-08:00","id":31140,"title":"","content":"Dude, seriously, just make the size either feet or yards in radius equal to Primium. Were this exalted even that would be ridiculous.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimethe